hifi-receiver licences
======================

This repository holds hardware, our own code and documents, firmware patches
and a little third-party material. Each part has its own licence. The full
licence texts are in LICENSES/.

Hardware: CERN-OHL-P-2.0 (LICENSES/CERN-OHL-P-2.0.txt)
  boards/     KiCad sources, schematics, layouts, Gerbers, renders and
              reports, except the aiee libraries named below
  enclosure/  case CAD sources and their outputs (STL, 3MF, renders)

Our own code and documents: MIT (the text is at the end of this file and in
LICENSES/MIT.txt)
  app/, bench/, tools/, docs/
  firmware/components/hifi/, firmware/board/, firmware/test/, firmware/tools/
  firmware/README.md, firmware/fw.json, firmware/upstream.lock
  everything else in this repository not named in this file

Firmware patches: each change takes the licence of the file it changes
  firmware/patches/      changes to squeezelite-esp32. squeezelite's own
                         files are GPL-3.0-or-later. squeezelite-esp32's
                         ESP32 files are mostly MIT. The libraries it
                         carries keep their own terms. The header of each
                         changed file decides. New files that a patch adds
                         are ours and MIT.
  firmware/idf-patches/  changes to ESP-IDF v4.4.8. Most of its files are
                         Apache-2.0 (LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt). lwIP and
                         wpa_supplicant files are BSD-3-Clause. The header
                         of each changed file decides.

Not ours: these keep their own terms
  firmware/third_party/libmad/src/ and .../patches/
              libmad 0.15.1b and the patches to it (Debian's fixes and our
              port changes), GPL-2.0-or-later (its own COPYING; also
              LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt). Our README.md there is MIT.
  boards/*/lib/aiee.pretty/, boards/*/lib/aiee.3dshapes/, boards/*/lib/aiee.kicad_sym
              footprints, symbols and 3D models made by easyeda2kicad from
              EasyEDA / LCSC part data, as their headers say. The licences
              above do not cover them; they keep whatever terms their
              source sets.

Firmware builds: GPL-3.0 (LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt)
  A firmware image built from this repository links squeezelite, so the
  image as a whole is distributed under version 3 of the GNU General Public
  License. squeezelite's own files allow any later version. Our MIT files in
  the image stay MIT, and you may reuse them on their own under MIT. Each
  published image names its exact source: this repository's commit,
  firmware/upstream.lock (the squeezelite-esp32 commit and the ESP-IDF
  version), the patches, and the build steps in firmware/README.md.

Copyright holders: the hifi-receiver authors (Hive-RSI-Lab). Third-party
files keep their own copyright notices.

